00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:11.637
-Yeah, sure. So, I --

00:01:11.637 --> 00:01:14.107
Thank you, by the way, man.
I appreciate it.

00:01:15.908 --> 00:01:18.277
I play Eddie Palmer, who --
when the movie begins,

00:01:18.277 --> 00:01:22.682
I'm coming back from
a 12-year stint in prison.

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:25.552
And as the movie progresses,
you kind of, find out more

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:27.386
about how I ended up there.

00:01:27.386 --> 00:01:32.192
But come back to a small town
in Louisiana,

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:37.096
and, you know, just a guy trying
to get his life back together,

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:38.664
searching for some sort of
redemption,

00:01:38.664 --> 00:01:45.538
and ends up in a situation
where a young boy

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:48.274
who, you know,
has a single mother

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.175
with a substance abuse problem,

00:01:50.175 --> 00:01:52.478
ends up abandoning him

00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:57.149
and kind of ends up in this guy,
you know.

00:01:57.149 --> 00:01:58.351
-In his life.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.718
-This guy ends up having to
take care of him.

00:01:59.718 --> 00:02:01.821
-The kid is fantastic,
by the way.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:04.023
-Yeah, he's --
in his first film.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:06.558
-I was gonna say,
where is he from?

00:02:06.558 --> 00:02:09.395
-Yeah, his name is Ryder Allen,
and it's his first film,

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:12.131
and he just -- he blew us away.

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:13.566
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:17.536
We -- We auditioned
a ton of kids,

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:19.471
and so many of them
were amazing,

00:02:19.471 --> 00:02:22.508
but he just kind of, like --
he showed up

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:23.710
and was just kind of like...

00:02:24.743 --> 00:02:27.013
You know, like,
he had this, like,

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:31.116
unabashed, you know --
-Yeah.

00:02:31.116 --> 00:02:34.520
-It was like he was
like a soda can opened up.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.021
It was just like "Boom!"

00:02:36.021 --> 00:02:39.759
And we just knew we had
something special with him.

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:42.862
And great
with improvisation, too.

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.564
-Yeah, and was he cool
with you being, like,

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:47.266
kind of not you?

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:49.602
I mean, because meeting
Justin Timberlake, you're like,

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:50.836
"Oh, my God, fun,"
but then you're like,

00:02:50.836 --> 00:02:53.306
"But I have to be mean."

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:56.842
-Well, this is [Laughs]
This is interesting.

00:02:56.842 --> 00:03:00.980
He actually didn't know
much about me.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:05.117
I mean, like you said,
I'm 40 now.

00:03:05.117 --> 00:03:07.820
-Yeah, he's --
-But he --

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.456
[ Chuckling ]
But he told me his mom did.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:11.757
-There you go.

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:14.160
-So that joke played well
throughout the whole shoot.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.895
I was like,
"Ask your mom about me."

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:18.797
No. No, no, no. I'm kidding.

00:03:18.797 --> 00:03:22.168
But it was actually great,

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:24.470
because we developed
a real bond.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:27.707
And I have become friends
with his family.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.475
-You see it growing
through the movie.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:32.044
You go, "Oh, my gosh,"
and then you go --

00:03:32.044 --> 00:03:35.214
By the end, you go, "Dude,"
it's a -- Whew!

00:03:35.214 --> 00:03:40.152
-Yeah, it's an emotional --
it's an emotional ride.

00:03:40.152 --> 00:03:44.590
And really touches
on some great themes, you know?

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:47.560
And it's timely.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.729
You know, it's a timely movie,
I think.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:52.398
-What do you want people
to take away from this film?

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:56.936
-Gosh, man.

00:03:56.936 --> 00:04:02.074
I mean, like I said,
it is about redemption.

00:04:02.074 --> 00:04:04.276
Self love. Acceptance.

00:04:04.276 --> 00:04:09.949
I think the theme of
acceptance -- you know,

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:14.487
'cause you meet this young boy,
and he likes what he likes.

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:16.289
-Yep.
-And it's not, you know,

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:21.327
stereotypical to what
the other kids around him like.

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:24.997
And, you know,
to watch these two

00:04:24.997 --> 00:04:29.802
kind of people from totally
different, you know, backgrounds

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:36.175
kind of come together and really
give each other meaning.

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:37.843
This young boy gets
a father figure.

00:04:37.843 --> 00:04:45.351
And my character, you know,
is taught this real --

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:50.789
I guess what it really means
to love somebody, you know,

00:04:50.789 --> 00:04:54.894
and, you know, accept them
for who they are, and...

00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:56.496
-But it's very like --
it's almost like,

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:59.498
"Hey, open your eyes
and start seeing everybody."

00:04:59.498 --> 00:05:00.766
It's --

00:05:00.766 --> 00:05:04.503
-Yes, see people
for who they are.

00:05:04.503 --> 00:05:08.574
And, yeah, open your eyes,

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:10.143
open your ears, open your heart.

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:12.378
-Yeah.
-That type of thing.

